# Perf flavour overlay for the a34x Image (PERF_FLAVOR=true).
#
# The default build keeps Samsung's debug instrumentation, which is what the
# stock 6.6.50 modules were built with. This overlay is only merged when the
# workflow is asked for the perf flavour, so both variants stay available.
#
# What and why:
#   UBSAN_*  every array index in the whole kernel gets a bounds check
#            (UBSAN_SANITIZE_ALL), and UBSAN_TRAP turns a detected overflow
#            into a panic. With PANIC_ON_OOPS=y and panic_timeout=-1 that is a
#            hung phone, not a reboot. Costs CPU on every syscall/IO path.
#   KFENCE   sampled heap checker: one static-branch test per allocation plus a
#            timer. Keep it when hunting memory bugs, drop it for a daily driver.
#   PAGE_OWNER / DEBUG_MEMORY_INIT  boot-time/zero-cost debug plumbing.
#   SCHEDSTATS  per-task scheduler accounting on enqueue/dequeue/migrate.
#
# Deliberately NOT touched here:
#   KASAN(_HW_TAGS)  already free: no MTE on MT6877, kasan never initialises.
#   CFI_CLANG, SHADOW_CALL_STACK, ARM64_PTR_AUTH, HARDENED_USERCOPY, FORTIFY
#                    security hardening, keep.
#   INIT_ON_ALLOC_DEFAULT_ON  already cancelled at runtime by init_on_alloc=0.

# CONFIG_UBSAN is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_TRAP is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_SANITIZE_ALL is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_LOCAL_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_SHIFT is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_UNREACHABLE is not set

# CONFIG_KFENCE is not set

# CONFIG_PAGE_OWNER is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_MEMORY_INIT is not set

# CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS is not set
